speechtext:
This afternoon we shall resume consideration of Bill C-83. You are aware, Mr. Speaker, that the House must take under consideration objections which have been filed respecting the provisions of the reports of the Electoral Boundaries Commissions. Discussions have taken place among representatives of the parties, and as a result I should like to propose an order of the House which would set the process in train. The time for taking into consideration the objections filed to the Nova Scotia redistribution expires tonight; that in respect of British Columbia expires on March 27; and that in respect of Alberta, on April 3.
It will be my intention to ask the House to set aside some time later for the consideration of all the objections which will have been filed by March 28, which I am given to understand is the final date for the filing of objections. This would include any of the objections to be discussed later today, the consideration of which is not completed. I should, therefore, like to move, seconded by my colleague, the Minister of Public Works:
That at 8:00 p.m. this day the House shall take up consideration of objections to the report of the Electoral Boundaries Commission for the province of Nova Scotia;
That, after completion of consideration of the said report, the House shall take up consideration of objections to the report of the Electoral Boundaries Commission for the British Columbia, but, if consideration of the report for Nova Scotia has not been completed at 8:40 p.m., the said consideration shall be adjourned and the House shall proceed forthwith to consideration of the report for British Columbia; and
That, after completion of consideration of the said report for British Columbia, the House shall take up consideration of objections to the report of the Electoral Boundaries Commission for Alberta, but, if consideration of the report for British Columbia has not been completed at 9:20 p.m., the said consideration shall be adjourned and the House shall proceed forthwith to consideration of the report for Alberta;
March 11, 1976

That at 8:00 p.m. this day the House shall take up consideration of objections to the report of the Electoral Boundaries Commission for the province of Nova Scotia;
